## Mechanical Indicators

Certain mechanical events (dice rolls, etc.) occurred this turn, as
listed below. Each is represented by a *marker* — a token of the form
`[MECH:...]` standing for the event (which is described after each
marker below). After you respond, the engine replaces each marker with
canonical formatted text (e.g. `**[STR check: failed]**`); the player
never sees the marker itself.

You MUST place EVERY marker below inside your narration, each exactly
once, at the narratively appropriate point — typically immediately
before the text describing the consequence of that event.

Place each marker on its own line, surrounded by blank lines (`\n\n`),
like this:

```
You strain hard, trying to lift the statue.

[MECH:check:0]

It's too heavy to budge.
```

Copy each marker verbatim — do not retype, renumber, or paraphrase it.

